       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your authority to prescribe isn't in question. The problem is that 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is well past the dose where benefit levels off. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise sharply. I don't know of a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate, and I'd rather not put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the usual maximum. I can add a note such as \"Max dose; monitor renal function and GI symptoms.\"\n- **Enter a different dose or frequency** if you tell me what you're trying to achieve.\n- **Add other pain control.** If 3,200 mg/day isn't enough, adding acetaminophen or another agent usually works better than a higher ibuprofen dose.\n\nIf you think this dose is truly warranted, for example under a specific protocol, please talk to the pharmacist or attending first. It should go through a pharmacy-reviewed pathway, not be entered by me.\n\nWhich of the options above would you like?"
      }
